# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What must never be committed, and why.
#
# Two of these matter more than the rest:
#
#   backend/storage/  holds uploaded resumes and the database built from them.
#                     That is other people's personal data - names, phone
#                     numbers, email addresses, academic records. It does not
#                     belong in version control, and once pushed it is very
#                     hard to remove from history. See the consent rules in
#                     docs/Customer Testing Plan.md.
#
#   backend/.env      holds real configuration, and is the file that will hold
#                     a secret the first time this is deployed anywhere.
#                     .env.example is committed instead, with every setting
#                     documented and no real values in it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Personal data and runtime state ---------------------------------------
backend/storage/
backend/artifacts/

# --- Configuration ----------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Node / frontend --------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- Logs -------------------------------------------------------------------
# The backend writes these when started with output redirected. They are local
# diagnostics, they can contain uploaded text, and they are never useful to
# anyone else.
*.log
*.err

# --- Obsidian ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The vault's content is committed - it is half the project. Only the
# per-machine UI state is not: which panes were open, where the cursor was.
# Committing those produces a merge conflict every time two people open the
# vault without either of them having changed a note.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/cache
.obsidian/graph.json

# --- Editors and operating systems ------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
